    "body": "## What does this implement/fix?\n\nFirmware release metadata and firmware assets were downloaded through a custom `TLSSocketFactory`. That helper was originally added to enable TLS 1.2 on Android versions older than 5.0.\n\nThe app now requires Android 8.0 or newer, where this compatibility workaround is no longer needed. Keeping it adds a custom TLS policy to firmware downloads without providing compatibility for supported devices.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Remove `TLSSocketFactory`.\n- Use the platform `HttpsURLConnection` defaults when fetching the firmware release list.\n- Use the platform `HttpsURLConnection` defaults when downloading firmware assets.\n\nThis keeps the existing HTTPS certificate and hostname validation behavior while allowing the platform to negotiate its supported TLS version.\n\n## Verification\n\nRelease-list fetching and firmware asset downloads should be checked on a supported Android 8.0+ device before merge.",
